{"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/grdbpersistence"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence"},"abstract":[{"text":"Keep each record in a table of the app’s own GRDB database until it is delivered.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"role":"collection","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"GRDBPersistence"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"GRDBPersistence","title":"GRDBPersistence"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabaseStore"},{"type":"text","text":" is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RecordStore"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence"},{"type":"text","text":") for apps on Apple platforms that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already keep a GRDB database. It takes the app’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabaseQueue"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabasePool"},{"type":"text","text":" and a table"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"name, creates the table with a migration of its own, and opens no second SQLite database. It is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"product of its own, which "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves out."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It makes the same promises as ","type":"text"},{"code":"SegmentStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The tracker’s worker commits each record, in a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"transaction of its own, before publishing it. A batch’s rows are marked before any destination","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"receives it and deleted once every destination has. The table holds at most ","type":"text"},{"code":"byteBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" bytes of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encoded records, 5 MiB by default, with the oldest rows deleted to make room, and each drop is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reported on ","type":"text"},{"code":"DatabaseStore.dropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Records are encoded as ","type":"text"},{"code":"SegmentStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" encodes them, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the same events are kept: every ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the program and the library’s own, or only the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" types ","type":"text"},{"code":"DatabaseStore(events:database:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lists. Rows written by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Traffluent 0.0.44 or earlier, in an earlier encoding, aren’t read: each is deleted when the store","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"opens and reported as ","type":"text"},{"code":".undecodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or as ","type":"text"},{"code":".versionMismatch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" where its stored version differs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from its type’s.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"How durable a commit is against power loss is the database’s choice, through its journal mode and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"synchronous"},{"type":"text","text":" setting. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabaseStore.synchronize()"},{"type":"text","text":" checkpoints a database in WAL mode; call it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as the app moves to the background. Open one store per table at a time, and don’t open one from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inside an access to the same database."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once a delivered record’s row is deleted, and in WAL mode once a later "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"synchronize()"},{"type":"text","text":" succeeds,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing of it is left in the database’s main file or its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-wal"},{"type":"text","text":" file. The store’s deletes run"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with SQLite’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"secure_delete"},{"type":"text","text":" ON and its inserts with at least FAST, so freed pages and moved rows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are zeroed, and the app’s own setting is put back after each. In WAL mode, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"synchronize()"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"truncates the log, which until then holds the deleted rows’ earlier bytes. While another"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"connection reads or writes the database, such as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabasePool"},{"type":"text","text":" read whose transaction is still"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"open, the log can’t be truncated, and the delivered records’ bytes, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" values and session"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"included, stay in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-wal"},{"type":"text","text":" file until a later "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"synchronize()"},{"type":"text","text":" runs after that connection is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"done. Inside a transaction, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"synchronize()"},{"type":"text","text":" checkpoints nothing."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing is promised outside those two files: a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-journal"},{"type":"text","text":" the app keeps with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"journal_mode=PERSIST"},{"type":"text","text":" can hold earlier rows’ bytes, and the file system may keep the blocks a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"truncated or deleted file gave up. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabaseStore"},{"type":"text","text":"’s documentation covers how long"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"synchronize()"},{"type":"text","text":" waits under each busy mode, and how a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabasePool"},{"type":"text","text":" empties the log itself."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An app with no database of its own uses "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentStore"},{"type":"text","text":", which needs no GRDB."}]},{"code":["import GRDB","import GRDBPersistence","","let database = try DatabaseQueue(path: databasePath)","let store = try DatabaseStore(database: database, table: \"analyticsRecord\")","let tracker = Tracker(store: store)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: vendor)","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what a store keeps, its bounds and recovery.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"API","anchor":"API","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The documentation site is built on Linux, where this module’s API isn’t there, so its symbols"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"have no pages of their own here. Their doc comments are in the sources, and Xcode shows them"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for an Apple target."}]},{"text":"Keeping records in a database","anchor":"Keeping-records-in-a-database","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabaseStore"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabaseStoreError"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://GRDBPersistence/documentation/GRDBPersistence":{"title":"GRDBPersistence","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/grdbpersistence","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep each record in a table of the app’s own GRDB database until it is delivered."}]},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/persistingrecords":{"type":"link","title":"Persisting Records","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Persisting Records","type":"text"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so the records a tracker tracked survive the app ending."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","title":"Persistence","role":"collection","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/persistence","kind":"symbol"}}}